# 必考词 Unit24
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit24核心词汇

{{design}}{{/dɪˈzaɪn}}{{v./n. 设计； design；图案}}{{She designed the logo for the company.}}
{{desire}}{{/dɪˈzaɪər}}{{n./v. 欲望； desire；渴望}}{{He has a strong desire to succeed.}}
{{desperate}}{{/ˈdespərət}}{{adj. 绝望的； desperate；不顾一切的}}{{The refugees were in desperate need of food and water.}}
{{despite}}{{/dɪˈspaɪt}}{{prep. 尽管； despite}}{{Despite the rain, the event was a success.}}
{{destiny}}{{/ˈdestəni}}{{n. 命运； destiny}}{{She believed it was her destiny to become a teacher.}}
{{detect}}{{/dɪˈtekt}}{{v. 检测； detect；发现}}{{The sensor can detect changes in temperature.}}
{{deteriorate}}{{/dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt}}{{v. 恶化； deteriorate}}{{His health deteriorated rapidly.}}
{{determine}}{{/dɪˈtɜːmɪn}}{{v. 决定； determine；确定}}{{The results will determine the next steps.}}
{{device}}{{/dɪˈvaɪs}}{{n. 设备； device；装置}}{{The device is used to measure air quality.}}
{{devote}}{{/dɪˈvəʊt}}{{v. 致力于； devote；奉献}}{{She devoted her career to medical research.}}
{{diagnose}}{{/ˈdaɪəɡnəʊz}}{{v. 诊断； diagnose}}{{The doctor diagnosed the illness early.}}
{{differ}}{{/ˈdɪfər}}{{v. 不同； differ；意见不同}}{{Opinions differ on this issue.}}
{{digest}}{{/daɪˈdʒest}}{{v./n. 消化； digest；摘要}}{{The food is difficult to digest.}}
{{dilemma}}{{/dɪˈlemə}}{{n. 困境； dilemma；两难}}{{He faced a moral dilemma.}}
{{dimension}}{{/daɪˈmenʃn}}{{n. 维度； dimension；方面}}{{The problem has many dimensions.}}
{{diminish}}{{/dɪˈmɪnɪʃ}}{{v. 减少； diminish；缩小}}{{The influence of the party has diminished.}}
{{diploma}}{{/dɪˈpləʊmə}}{{n. 毕业文凭； diploma；学位证书}}{{She earned a diploma in business administration.}}
{{diplomatic}}{{/ˌdɪpləˈmætɪk}}{{adj. 外交的； diplomatic；老练的}}{{The diplomatic negotiations lasted for months.}}
{{disabled}}{{/dɪsˈeɪbld}}{{adj. 残疾的； disabled}}{{The building has facilities for disabled people.}}
{{discipline}}{{/ˈdɪsəplɪn}}{{n./v. 纪律； discipline；学科}}{{The school has strict discipline policies.}}
{{disclose}}{{/dɪsˈkləʊz}}{{v. 披露； disclose；揭露}}{{The company refused to disclose the information.}}
{{discount}}{{/ˈdɪskaʊnt}}{{n./v. 折扣； discount；忽视}}{{The store offers a 20% discount on all items.}}
{{discourse}}{{/ˈdɪskɔːs}}{{n. 论述； discourse；话语}}{{The academic discourse on climate change is extensive.}}
{{discover}}{{/dɪˈskʌvər}}{{v. 发现； discover}}{{Scientists discovered a new species of fish.}}
{{discriminate}}{{/dɪˈskrɪmɪneɪt}}{{v. 歧视； discriminate；区分}}{{It is illegal to discriminate against people based on gender.}}
{{disguise}}{{/dɪsˈɡaɪz}}{{v./n. 伪装； disguise；假装}}{{He disguised himself as a police officer.}}
{{dismiss}}{{/dɪsˈmɪs}}{{v. 解雇； dismiss；驳回}}{{The judge dismissed the case.}}
{{disorder}}{{/dɪsˈɔːdər}}{{n. 混乱； disorder；疾病}}{{She suffers from a sleep disorder.}}
{{display}}{{/dɪˈspleɪ}}{{v./n. 展示； display；陈列}}{{The museum displays artifacts from ancient Egypt.}}
{{dispose}}{{/dɪˈspəʊz}}{{v. 处理； dispose；丢弃}}{{The waste was disposed of safely.}}
{{dispute}}{{/dɪˈspjuːt}}{{n./v. 争端； dispute；争论}}{{The dispute was resolved through mediation.}}
{{disrupt}}{{/dɪsˈrʌpt}}{{v. 扰乱； disrupt；中断}}{{The strike disrupted transportation services.}}
{{dissolve}}{{/dɪˈzɒlv}}{{v. 溶解； dissolve；解散}}{{Sugar dissolves in hot water.}}
{{distinct}}{{/dɪˈstɪŋkt}}{{adj. 明显的； distinct；独特的}}{{There are two distinct approaches to the problem.}}
{{distinguish}}{{/dɪˈstɪŋɡwɪʃ}}{{v. 区分； distinguish；辨别}}{{It is hard to distinguish between the two products.}}
{{distort}}{{/dɪˈstɔːt}}{{v. 歪曲； distort；扭曲}}{{The media distorted the facts.}}
{{distribute}}{{/dɪˈstrɪbjuːt}}{{v. 分配； distribute；分发}}{{The food was distributed to the refugees.}}
{{disturb}}{{/dɪˈstɜːb}}{{v. 打扰； disturb；扰乱}}{{Please do not disturb me while I'm studying.}}
{{diverse}}{{/daɪˈvɜːs}}{{adj. 多样的； diverse；不同的}}{{The city has a diverse population.}}
{{divert}}{{/daɪˈvɜːt}}{{v. 转移； divert；使转向}}{{Traffic was diverted to another road.}}
{{divine}}{{/dɪˈvaɪn}}{{adj. 神圣的； divine；极好的}}{{The ancient temple was considered a divine place.}}
{{document}}{{/ˈdɒkjumənt}}{{n./v. 文件； document；记录}}{{Please document all expenses carefully.}}
{{domestic}}{{/dəˈmestɪk}}{{adj. 国内的； domestic；家庭的}}{{The government focuses on domestic issues.}}
{{dominant}}{{/ˈdɒmɪnənt}}{{adj. 主导的； dominant；占优势的}}{{English is the dominant language in international business.}}
{{dominate}}{{/ˈdɒmɪneɪt}}{{v. 支配； dominate；占主导地位}}{{The company dominates the market.}}
{{donate}}{{/dəʊˈneɪt}}{{v. 捐赠； donate；捐献}}{{She donated a large sum to charity.}}
{{dose}}{{/dəʊs}}{{n. 剂量； dose；一剂}}{{The doctor prescribed a low dose of the medication.}}
{{draft}}{{/drɑːft}}{{n./v. 草稿； draft；起草}}{{She submitted the first draft of her thesis.}}
{{dramatic}}{{/drəˈmætɪk}}{{adj. 戏剧性的； dramatic；引人注目的}}{{There has been a dramatic increase in online shopping.}}
{{drift}}{{/drɪft}}{{v./n. 漂流； drift；趋势}}{{The boat drifted down the river.}}
{{drought}}{{/draʊt}}{{n. 干旱； drought}}{{The drought destroyed many crops.}}
{{dull}}{{/dʌl}}{{adj. 枯燥的； dull；钝的}}{{The lecture was dull and uninteresting.}}
{{dump}}{{/dʌmp}}{{v./n. 倾倒； dump；垃圾场}}{{Companies should not dump waste into rivers.}}
{{durable}}{{/ˈdjʊərəbl}}{{adj. 耐用的； durable}}{{The material is very durable.}}
{{duration}}{{/djʊˈreɪʃn}}{{n. 持续时间； duration}}{{The duration of the course is six months.}}
{{dynamic}}{{/daɪˈnæmɪk}}{{adj. 动态的； dynamic；有活力的}}{{The city has a dynamic economy.}}
{{economy}}{{/ɪˈkɒnəmi}}{{n. 经济； economy；节约}}{{The economy is showing signs of recovery.}}
{{edition}}{{/ɪˈdɪʃn}}{{n. 版次； edition；版本}}{{The third edition of the book was published last year.}}
{{elaborate}}{{/ɪˈlæbərət}}{{adj./v. 精心的； elaborate；详细阐述}}{{Could you elaborate on your proposal?}}
{{elect}}{{/ɪˈlekt}}{{v. 选举； elect；选择}}{{She was elected president of the student council.}}
{{element}}{{/ˈelɪmənt}}{{n. 元素； element；要素；成分}}{{Trust is an essential element of a good relationship.}}
{{eliminate}}{{/ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt}}{{v. 消除； eliminate；淘汰}}{{The company aims to eliminate waste.}}
{{elite}}{{/eɪˈliːt}}{{n./adj. 精英； elite；精英的}}{{The school is known for educating the elite.}}
{{embrace}}{{/ɪmˈbreɪs}}{{v./n. 拥抱； embrace；接受}}{{The company embraced new technology.}}
{{emerge}}{{/ɪˈmɜːdʒ}}{{v. 出现； emerge；浮现}}{{New evidence emerged during the investigation.}}
{{emergency}}{{/ɪˈmɜːdʒənsi}}{{n. 紧急情况； emergency}}{{In case of emergency, call 112.}}
{{emit}}{{/ɪˈmɪt}}{{v. 发出； emit；排放}}{{The factory emits large amounts of carbon dioxide.}}
{{emotion}}{{/ɪˈməʊʃn}}{{n. 情感； emotion；情绪}}{{She tried to hide her emotions.}}
{{emphasis}}{{/ˈemfəsɪs}}{{n. 强调； emphasis；重点}}{{The school places great emphasis on reading.}}
{{empire}}{{/ˈempaɪər}}{{n. 帝国； empire；大企业}}{{The Roman Empire lasted for centuries.}}
{{enable}}{{/ɪˈneɪbl}}{{v. 使能够； enable；使可能}}{{Technology enables people to work from home.}}
{{encounter}}{{/ɪnˈkaʊntər}}{{v./n. 遇到； encounter；遭遇}}{{She encountered many difficulties during the project.}}
{{encourage}}{{/ɪnˈkʌrɪdʒ}}{{v. 鼓励； encourage；促进}}{{The teacher encouraged students to ask questions.}}
{{endure}}{{/ɪnˈdjʊər}}{{v. 忍受； endure；持续}}{{She endured years of hardship.}}
{{enforce}}{{/ɪnˈfɔːs}}{{v. 执行； enforce；强制实施}}{{The police enforce the law strictly.}}
{{engage}}{{/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒ}}{{v. 从事； engage；吸引}}{{The students were engaged in the discussion.}}
{{enhance}}{{/ɪnˈhɑːns}}{{v. 增强； enhance；提高}}{{The new software enhances productivity.}}
{{enormous}}{{/ɪˈnɔːməs}}{{adj. 巨大的； enormous}}{{The project requires an enormous investment.}}
{{enrich}}{{/ɪnˈrɪtʃ}}{{v. 丰富； enrich；使富裕}}{{Travel enriches the mind.}}
{{ensure}}{{/ɪnˈʃʊər}}{{v. 确保； ensure}}{{Please ensure that all doors are locked.}}
{{enterprise}}{{/ˈentəpraɪz}}{{n. 企业； enterprise；进取心}}{{The government supports small enterprises.}}
{{enthusiasm}}{{/ɪnˈθjuːziæzəm}}{{n. 热情； enthusiasm}}{{She showed great enthusiasm for the project.}}
{{entire}}{{/ɪnˈtaɪər}}{{adj. 全部的； entire；整个的}}{{He spent the entire day reading.}}
{{entity}}{{/ˈentəti}}{{n. 实体； entity；存在}}{{The company is a separate legal entity.}}
{{environment}}{{/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt}}{{n. 环境； environment}}{{Protecting the environment is everyone's responsibility.}}
{{episode}}{{/ˈepɪsəʊd}}{{n. 一集； episode；事件}}{{The final episode of the series was exciting.}}
{{equal}}{{/ˈiːkwəl}}{{adj./v./n. 相等的； equal；等于}}{{All citizens are equal before the law.}}
{{equip}}{{/ɪˈkwɪp}}{{v. 装备； equip；使有能力}}{{The school is equipped with modern facilities.}}
{{equivalent}}{{/ɪˈkwɪvələnt}}{{adj./n. 等同的； equivalent；等价物}}{{One mile is roughly equivalent to 1.6 kilometers.}}
{{era}}{{/ˈɪərə}}{{n. 时代； era；纪元}}{{We are living in the digital era.}}
{{erode}}{{/ɪˈrəʊd}}{{v. 侵蚀； erode；削弱}}{{Public trust in the government has been eroded.}}
{{error}}{{/ˈerər}}{{n. 错误； error；过失}}{{The report contained several errors.}}
{{escape}}{{/ɪˈskeɪp}}{{v./n. 逃跑； escape；逃避}}{{The prisoners escaped from jail.}}
{{essential}}{{/ɪˈsenʃl}}{{adj. 必要的； essential；本质的}}{{Sleep is essential for good health.}}
{{establish}}{{/ɪˈstæblɪʃ}}{{v. 建立； establish；确立}}{{The university was established in 1900.}}
{{estimate}}{{/ˈestɪmeɪt}}{{v./n. 估计； estimate；估算}}{{The cost is estimated at $5 million.}}
{{evaluate}}{{/ɪˈvæljueɪt}}{{v. 评估； evaluate；评价}}{{The committee will evaluate the proposals.}}
{{eventually}}{{/ɪˈventʃuəli}}{{adv. 最终； eventually}}{{Eventually, they reached an agreement.}}
{{evidence}}{{/ˈevɪdəns}}{{n. 证据； evidence；迹象}}{{There is strong evidence to support the theory.}}
{{evolve}}{{/ɪˈvɒlv}}{{v. 进化； evolve；逐步发展}}{{The company has evolved over the past decade.}}
{{exaggerate}}{{/ɪɡˈzædʒəreɪt}}{{v. 夸大； exaggerate}}{{He tends to exaggerate his achievements.}}
{{exceed}}{{/ɪkˈsiːd}}{{v. 超过； exceed；超越}}{{The results exceeded our expectations.}}
